answer:
Verdict: bug found

Line 11: `if (balance<amount) return NULL;`

The insufficient-funds path leaves m held, omitting its exit section.

| Step | Thread A | Thread B | Shared state |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | lock(m) succeeds |  | m=A, balance=40 |
| 2 | test balance < 45 -> true |  | m=A |
| 3 | return without unlock |  | m still owned by exited A |
| 4 |  | lock(m) blocks | B cannot complete |

Fix:
```diff
--- prog.c
+++ prog.c (fixed)
@@ -8,7 +8,7 @@
 static int balance=40;
 static void *withdraw(void *arg) {
     int amount=*(int *)arg; pthread_mutex_lock(&m);
-    if (balance<amount) return NULL;
+    if (balance<amount) { pthread_mutex_unlock(&m); return NULL; }
     balance-=amount; pthread_mutex_unlock(&m); return NULL;
 }
 int main(void) {
```

The rejected path now releases the mutex before returning, so every successful entry has one exit. The valid withdrawal can then complete under the same protection.

