answer:
Verdict: bug found

Line 12: `if (ready==0) pthread_cond_wait(&cv,&m);`

The if guard tests once. An allowed spurious return permits the assertion or later consumption even when ready is still zero.

| Step | Thread A | Thread B | Shared state |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | lock(m) succeeds |  | m=A, ready=0 |
| 2 | read ready -> 0 |  | m=A |
| 3 | cond_wait: release-and-wait |  | A waiting; B not yet scheduled |
| 4 | cond_wait returns spuriously, reacquiring m |  | m=A, ready=0 |
| 5 | assert ready equals expected fails |  | no predicate recheck; ready=0 |

Fix:
```diff
--- prog.c
+++ prog.c (fixed)
@@ -9,7 +9,7 @@
