```

The while guard re-evaluates ready after every return with m held. A false predicate goes back to waiting, including after spurious or competing-consumer wakeups.

question:
Is this 16-unit update's mutex entry section correct, or can I unlock first to make sure m is free? Assume successful API calls unless the ownership protocol itself is invalid.
```c
