answer:
Verdict: bug found

Line 11: `pthread_mutex_unlock(&m);`

The first unlock has no matching ownership. For a default mutex, you cannot rely on a portable useful result for an invalid non-owner unlock; this is a protocol violation even with one worker.

| Step | Thread A | Thread B | Shared state |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | unlock(m) without prior acquisition |  | m was free; A has no ownership |

Fix:
```diff
--- prog.c
+++ prog.c (fixed)
@@ -8,7 +8,7 @@
